<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fishbourne Roman Palace</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 75</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fishbourne Roman Palace, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chichester">Chichester</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-sussex">West Sussex</a>, is the largest known Roman residence in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, built around 75 with formal gardens and fine mosaics. Discovered in 1960, it has often been linked to the client king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/togidubnus">Togidubnus</a>. It burned down in the late 3rd century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fishbourne-roman-palace.jpg" alt="Fishbourne Roman Palace" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charlesdrakew · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fishbourne_palace_north_wing.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
